01:16:45,714 --> 01:16:51,714
Possession is a 1981 psychological horror drama film directed by
Andrzej Żuławski and written by Żuławski and Frederic Tuten.

14
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The plot obliquely follows the relationship between an international spy (Sam Neill) and his wife (Isabelle
Adjani), who begins exhibiting increasingly disturbing behavior after asking for a divorce.

15
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
Possession, an international co-production between France and
West Germany, was filmed in West Berlin in 1980.

16
01:34:28,571 --> 01:34:34,571
Żuławski's only English-language film, it premiered at the 34th Cannes Film
Festival, where Adjani won the Best Actress award for her performance.

17
01:40:22,857 --> 01:40:28,857
The screenplay was written during the painful divorce of
Żuławski from actress Małgorzata Braunek.

18
01:46:17,142 --> 01:46:23,142
While not commercially successful either in Europe or in the United States, with the latter only receiving a heavily edited cut on
its initial release, the film eventually acquired cult status and has been more positively appraised in later years.

19
01:52:11,428 --> 01:52:17,428
The film explores themes of adultery, berlin,
germany, monster, police, marriage crisis.

